## What changed

**New `src/tokenize.ts`** — the single tokenizer, extracted from `wordCount`'s behaviour:
```ts
export function tokenize(text: string): string[] {
  return text.toLowerCase().split(/[^a-z0-9']+/).filter((word) => word !== '')
}
```

**`src/stats.ts`**
- `wordCount` is now `tokenize(text).length` — same regex, same empty filter, so its results are unchanged (the original test still passes untouched).
- `topWords` now counts `tokenize`'s tokens (fixing the drift: case-insensitive, apostrophes kept inside words, punctuation/digits are separators rather than stripped), then sorts most-frequent-first with ties broken alphabetically, then slices to `n`:
  ```ts
  .sort((a, b) => b[1] - a[1] || (a[0] < b[0] ? -1 : 1))
  ```
  The sort is the only other behavioural delta besides the tokenizer: previously ties came out in insertion order.

**`src/stats.test.ts`** — kept the existing `wordCount` test, added coverage: `tokenize` (lower-casing, word-character class incl. `"2nd-rate"` → `2nd`,`rate` and `"o.k."` → `o`,`k`, empty input / separators-only → `[]`), and `topWords` (case-insensitivity `"The the THE"` → `[['the',3]]`, frequency-then-alphabetical ordering, `n` truncation at the tie boundary, `n` larger than the distinct words, apostrophe handling `"don't don't don.t"`).

